<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-19T19:58:06.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-lists-8e1f66d8-27f7-43af-9cad-e8dffcc7b0da",
        "text": "Sometimes, information is best presented as a list! HTML offers special elements to help us organize items clearly and make them easy to read.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/75c866b7da5b82893c8aa282e3d34713-test-lesson-intro-lists-panel-1-8872162f-3dba-4fc3-9235-4f82f1a27aa5.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-lists-2716ebe5-05f8-4ab0-89d8-030c526158e5",
        "text": "For items where the order doesn't matter, like a grocery list or a list of hobbies, we use an **unordered list** with the `<ul>` tag. Each item inside gets its own `<li>` (list item) tag.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/c64bea8cd68a6a576c3296e47c794d7a-test-lesson-intro-lists-panel-2-15c806a2-71eb-4084-a7f1-10aea10cf5e5.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-lists-d2e91591-632e-45ce-a590-fdcebde35798",
        "text": "When the order *does* matter, like steps in a recipe or instructions for a game, we use an **ordered list** with the `<ol>` tag. Just like before, each item uses an `<li>` tag.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/1fea85cc8252d80e03c25869edb7ac4f-test-lesson-intro-lists-panel-3-b725dcec-6aff-41c1-9cb2-812402c39e78.png",
        "layout": "text-top-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-intro-lists-ae1604dd-3980-43b9-a6ef-5a75366d9d06",
        "text": "So, `<ul>` gives you bullet points (unordered), and `<ol>` gives you numbers (ordered) by default. Both use `<li>` for the individual list items to structure your content!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/316281ee2d3285e32b1fbf49e0edd43c-test-lesson-intro-lists-panel-4-89d039e7-cc4c-4814-9761-a9ea61b58b9c.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      }
    ],
    "generate_prompt": "Introduce unordered lists (<ul>) and ordered lists (<ol>) along with list items (<li>). Explain their purpose in organizing information and when to use each type of list."
  },
  "published": true,
